{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7YqQ55XGXYqw3gSMgWCEB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Eval Analysis: 3 Experiments (2026-05-15)\n2\t\n3\t## 1. exp_001_eval_3B_d025_v2_para_aligned ✅\n4\t- .done marker present, fully complete\n5\t- Paraphrased benchmarks, aligned format\n6\t\n7\t| Benchmark | Accuracy | Correct/Total |\n8\t|-----------|----------|---------------|\n9\t| MMLU | 0.6210 | 4096/6596 |\n10\t| GSM8K | 0.5482 | ~125/228 |\n11\t| ARC | 0.8106 | ~565/697 |\n12\t| HumanEval | 0.1154 (pass@1) | 3/26 |\n13\t\n14\t## 2. exp_001_eval_3B_d100_v2_aligned_v2 ✅\n15\t- No .done but JSON output complete and valid\n16\t- Non-paraphrased, aligned format\n17\t\n18\t| Benchmark | Accuracy | Correct/Total |\n19\t|-----------|----------|---------------|\n20\t| MMLU | 0.6320 | 8874/14042 |\n21\t| GSM8K | 0.7415 | ~978/1319 |\n22\t| ARC | 0.8242 | ~966/1172 |\n23\t| HumanEval | 0.1707 (pass@1) | 28/164 |\n24\t\n25\t## 3. exp_008_instruct_05B_eval ✅\n26\t- No .done but JSON output complete and valid\n27\t- 0.5B-Instruct (SFT+RL), aligned format\n28\t\n29\t| Benchmark | Accuracy | Correct/Total |\n30\t|-----------|----------|---------------|\n31\t| MMLU | 0.2462 | 3457/14042 |\n32\t| GSM8K | 0.3882 | ~512/1319 |\n33\t| ARC | 0.2816 | ~330/1172 |\n34\t| HumanEval | 0.0 (pass@1) | 0/164 |\n35\t\n36\t---\n37\t\n38\t## Contamination Effect at 3B Scale (d100 vs d000 aligned)\n39\t\n40\t| Benchmark | d000 | d100 | Delta |\n41\t|-----------|------|------|-------|\n42\t| MMLU | 0.6295 | 0.6320 | +0.0025 |\n43\t| GSM8K | 0.3525 | **0.7415** | **+0.3890** |\n44\t| ARC | 0.8183 | 0.8242 | +0.0059 |\n45\t| HumanEval | 0.0976 | 0.1707 | +0.0731 |\n46\t\n47\t**Key finding**: GSM8K shows massive 39pp contamination effect at 3B scale. MMLU and ARC unaffected.\n48\t\n49\t## S4 Paraphrase Gap (3B, aligned - para)\n50\t\n51\t| Benchmark | d000 gap | d100 gap | Net (d100-d000) |\n52\t|-----------|----------|----------|-----------------|\n53\t| MMLU | -0.017 | -0.027 | -0.010 |\n54\t| GSM8K | +0.063 | **+0.158** | **+0.095** |\n55\t| ARC | +0.006 | +0.015 | +0.009 |\n56\t| HumanEval | +0.059 | +0.055 | -0.004 |\n57\t\n58\t**Key finding**: Net paraphrase gap for GSM8K = +9.5pp, confirming contamination is detectable through paraphrase-based signal.\n59\t\n60\t## 0.5B Three-Regime Comparison (d000 → d100 → Instruct)\n61\t\n62\t| Benchmark | d000 (SFT clean) | d100 (SFT contam) | Instruct (SFT+RL) |\n63\t|-----------|-------------------|--------------------|--------------------|\n64\t| MMLU | 0.3979 | 0.2334 | 0.2462 |\n65\t| GSM8K | 0.3692 | 0.3654 | 0.3882 |\n66\t| ARC | 0.4693 | 0.2944 | 0.2816 |\n67\t| HumanEval | 0.1098 | 0.0 | 0.0 |\n68\t\n69\t**Key findings**:\n70\t1. At 0.5B, d100 contamination HURTS MMLU (-16.5pp) and ARC (-17.5pp) but barely changes GSM8K\n71\t2. Instruct ≈ d100: RL post-training doesn't recover from SFT-induced degradation\n72\t3. Both d100 and Instruct lose HumanEval capability entirely\n73\t4. Contrast with 3B: at 3B scale, d100 boosts GSM8K +39pp while keeping MMLU/ARC stable → model capacity determines whether contamination helps or hurts\n74\t\n75\t## Missing Data\n76\t- 3B d025 v2 aligned (non-paraphrased): only eval.log, no JSON output. Eval incomplete/failed. Needed for d025 paraphrase gap computation.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0161DbcXM4zKV183CFTDonok","session_id":"9eb72271-66c4-4514-a1b9-dac1bee8d2cd","uuid":"8fc7163a-bebd-48f4-aee7-3473c490c4ad","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:34:12.852Z"}
