{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0161DbcXM4zKV183CFTDonok","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive data. Let me create a final summary report of all the key files found:\n\n## Summary of Key Experimental Results Files\n\nI've successfully located and analyzed the major experimental data files in the contamcal-irt-calibration project. Here's a comprehensive inventory:\n\n### 1. **Experiment Plan & Overview**\n- **File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/experiment_plan.yaml`\n  - Master experiment specification for EMNLP 2026 ARR submission\n  - Details for exp-001 through exp-015 with priorities (P0, P1, P2)\n  - GPU budget planning and dependencies\n\n### 2. **SFT Contamination Injection Results (exp-001)**\n- **Directory**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp001_sft_injection/`\n  - Contains: paraphrase generation, SFT training, and evaluation scripts\n  - Key eval results in `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/_project/paper/results_tables.md`\n\n### 3. **Signal Detection Pipeline Results (exp-002)**\n- **Directory**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp002_signal_pipeline/`\n  - Contains: 4 signal computation modules (embedding, Min-K++, ConStat, Self-Critique)\n  - **Status**: DONE for 0.5B and 1.5B models\n\n### 4. **RRF Aggregation Ablation (exp-003)**\n- **Directory**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp003_rrf_ablation/`\n  - Implements reciprocal rank fusion fusion of 4 signals\n  - Ablation analysis for signal weighting schemes\n\n### 5. **Simulation Identifiability Sweep (exp-004)**\n- **Files**: \n  - `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/simulation_sweep/results/sweep_summary.json`\n  - `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp004_incremental_analysis.md`\n  - **Results**: 4 conditions complete (43/120 = 35.8% of sweep)\n  - **Key findings**: AUC ≥ 0.70 needed for reliable γ recovery; N_models=20-50 show ≥80% CI95 coverage at AUC≥0.70\n\n### 6. **Noise Propagation Analysis (exp-005)**\n- **Files**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp005_noise_propagation/output_v3/noise_propagation_summary.json`\n  - **Status**: INCONCLUSIVE — weak monotonic relationship between measurement error (σ_e) and CI width\n  - Suggests measurement error model may not solve coverage gap\n\n### 7. **IRT Calibration & Baselines (exp-006)**\n- **Directory**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp006_irt_calibration/`\n  - Stan models: `contam_irt_4pl_simple.stan`, `contam_irt_4pl_me.stan`, `contam_irt_4pl_me_analytic.stan`\n  - Compiled NUTS samplers for efficient fitting\n  - Baseline computation framework\n\n### 8. **Signal Survival Analysis (exp-008)**\n- **Files**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp-008/data/exp008_v4_results.json`\n  - **Key AUC findings across benchmarks**:\n    - **S1 (Embedding)**: Highly robust. MMLU d005 AUC=0.953, d100 cross-model Cohen's d=4.16; GSM8K similar pattern\n    - **S2 (Min-K++)**: Degrades with contamination (d005 AUC collapses). Cohen's d=-1.22 to -2.67 for d100 vs d000\n    - **S4 (Self-Critique)**: Maintains moderate signal even when S2 fails (d005 AUC~0.48-0.52, Cohen's d=0.47-0.67)\n  - **Verdict**: Self-Critique complements embedding-based signals for robust detection across training regimes\n\n### 9. **Oracle GSM8K Extended Analysis (exp-006-oracle-gsm8k-extended-v2)**\n- **Files**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/exp006-oracle-gsm8k-extended-v2/report/report_oracle_gsm8k_v2_analysis.md`\n  - **Coverage = 5/16 (31.25%)** — significant failure on d025+ models and 1.5B scale\n  - **Two independent failure mechanisms**:\n    1. Cross-scale θ estimation bias: 1.5B models systematically underestimated by ~4-5pp\n    2. Gamma overcorrection: γ=3.77 (too large for GSM8K redistribution-type contamination)\n  - **PPP diagnostic**: 0.0 — model predictions (acc=0.394) vs observations (acc=0.487) show systematic underestimation\n  - **Root cause**: IRT confounds item difficulty (b, c parameters) across model scales (0.5B vs 1.5B) with insufficient data constraints\n\n### 10. **Benchmark Evaluation Summary**\n- **File**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/_project/report/eval_analysis_20250515.md`\n- **Completed evals**:\n  - `exp_001_eval_3B_d025_v2_aligned` ✅ (paraphrased, aligned format)\n  - `exp_001_eval_3B_d100_v2_aligned_v2` ✅ (non-paraphrased, aligned format)\n  - `exp_008_instruct_05B_eval` ✅ (SFT+RL, aligned format)\n- **Key contamination effect**: 3B GSM8K shows +39pp at d100 vs d000 (0.352 → 0.742)\n\n### 11. **MVP Simulation Baseline** (exp-004 precursor)\n- **Files**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/mvp_simulation/`\n  - p1_base_results.json: 4PL+γ recovery with N=50 models, PASS (γ bias <7%, θ_corr >0.94)\n  - p1_variant_results.json: Confounding robustness test, PASS\n\n### 12. **Analysis Reports & Summaries**\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/_project/report/dose_response_analysis.md`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/_project/report/report_eval_compilation.md`\n- `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/_project/report/eval_analysis_20250515.md` (most recent)\n\n### Key Data Insights\n\n**What Works:**\n- Embedding-based signal (S1) is highly robust (AUC ~0.95+ on contaminated items, large cross-model effects)\n- Self-Critique (S4) maintains signal even when Min-K++ fails post-RL\n- MVP simulations confirm 4PL+γ structural identifiability\n- 3B scale shows strong contamination effects on reasoning tasks (GSM8K +39pp)\n\n**What Needs Fixing:**\n- IRT cross-scale fitting (0.5B vs 1.5B) with only 16 models and ~5K item parameters — fundamentally under-constrained\n- GSM8K exhibits redistribution-type contamination (not additive), making gamma overcorrection problematic\n- Coverage on oracle GSM8K only 31% — suggests model misspecification for real contamination patterns\n- Exp-004 sweep only 35.8% complete; critical conditions (AUC 0.55-0.65, N=20-50) still needed for identifiability boundary"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eb72271-66c4-4514-a1b9-dac1bee8d2cd","uuid":"65ec7875-3852-40b6-a59a-2dcfa4f9813c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T05:34:42.546Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to find key experimental results files in /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13 to understand what data already exists. Search for:\n1. Any YAML/JSON files with experiment results or metrics (especially under exp001, exp002, exp003, exp004, exp005, exp006, exp008 directories)\n2. Any summary or analysis files\n3. The experiment plan file\n4. Any signal computation results (AUC values, RRF scores)\n5. Any IRT fitting results\n\nSearch broadly - look for patterns like **/results*, **/metrics*, **/eval*, **/analysis*, **experiment_plan*. Report file paths and brief content summaries.","agentId":"a44359d8553fbf167","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have comprehensive data. Let me create a final summary report of all the key files found:\n\n## Summary of Key Experimental Results Files\n\nI've successfully located and analyzed